  "RightSideDisplay": 10,
  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>Downtime and recovery</h4><p>Compare this move's expected outage and data loss with the objectives for each affected mission/business process.</p><ul><li><b>MTD</b> - the total outage leaders are willing to accept, including all impact considerations.</li><li><b>RTO</b> - the maximum time a system resource can be unavailable before an unacceptable impact; normally shorter than the MTD.</li><li><b>RPO</b> - the point in time to which data can be recovered from the most recent backup; not part of the MTD.</li></ul><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Mission/business process</th><th>MTD</th><th>RTO</th><th>RPO</th></tr><tr><td>Pay vendor invoice (template example)</td><td>72 hours</td><td>48 hours</td><td>12 hours (last backup)</td></tr><tr><td>{your process}</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table><p><i>Source: NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1, Contingency Planning Guide for Federal Information Systems (2010), Section 3.2 and Appendix B (BIA template).</i></p>",
